{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122779-what-type-of-mage-stories-do-you-prefer-to-play","id":1122779,"title":"What type of Mage stories do you prefer to play?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T12:47:59-07:00","id":1122779,"title":"What type of Mage stories do you prefer to play?","content":"Our group really does do it all. Dark conspiracy city based, light hearted fantasy in the Dreaming, combative Sci-fi, you name it.<br /> <br /> As the primary ST for our group I prefer investigative dark conspiracy with minimal combat. Most of my stories go for 1 1/2 to 2 years and between 100 and 150 exp., which we all like as it allows for some lengthy indepth character development. <br /> <br /> How about you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T13:37:25-07:00","id":1122794,"title":"","content":"World-Spanning Strategy. Personally I find that a Mage game that doesn't span the entire globe is kind of squandering the potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:19:30-07:00","id":1122853,"title":"","content":"When I can get the time to actually run stuff, I prefer to aim for something along the personal scale and scope of stuff by William Gibson, Neil Stephenson, Dean Koontz, and Tim Powers, about how the individual deals with these revolutionary and often unsettling (if not outright frightening) ideas, as well as their own personal goals and baggage, before moving on to explore what they might mean for society as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:43:47-07:00","id":1123070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122779-what-type-of-mage-stories-do-you-prefer-to-play?p=1122853#post1122853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I can get the time to actually run stuff, I prefer to aim for something along the personal scale and scope of stuff by William Gibson, Neil Stephenson, Dean Koontz, and Tim Powers, about how the individual deals with these revolutionary and often unsettling (if not outright frightening) ideas, as well as their own personal goals and baggage, before moving on to explore what they might mean for society as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, definitely this. Personal games that are highly dependent on the PCs is what I find most enjoyable. Sometimes those evolve into larger scale games, but I always feel that PC first, story second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:44:57-07:00","id":1123071,"title":"","content":"Localized low powered street games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:12:47-07:00","id":1123193,"title":"","content":"Anything, really. Maybe I tend to lay a bit to the direction of at least some crossover and slightly more epicness (I just like to see some flash in a game about mages), but gritty street-level stuff has it's charms too (and frankly, I like best when there's the whole scale were presented at some point of a chronicle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-31-2017, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[